      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the board is **not** using deferred initialization and the board has an initialization order problem, this code will manually trigger the device init.\n\nThe [kernel](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/kernel/init.c;l\u003d243;drc\u003d954e29ed38a42fb5f4ff00c3845162c0ab5afb35) will also attempt initialization because it doesn\u0027t check the `initialized` flag.\n\nYou could check `dev-\u003eflags \u0026 DEVICE_FLAG_INIT_DEFERRED` as well.  If the flag is clear and the device isn\u0027t ready, generate an ASSERT.",
